   "text": "I read the drawing in four pieces and joined them.\n\n- **Left end:** a pyridazine carrying a 2-hydroxyphenyl group, an NH2 group, and a ring nitrogen link to a bicyclic amine.\n- **Bicyclic amine:** a 3,8-diazabicyclo[3.2.1]octane. N3 attaches to the pyridazine and the bridging N8 attaches to the pyrimidine.\n- **Linker:** a pyrimidine 2,5-disubstituted by the bridging N8 and a hex-5-ynamide chain, C#C\u2013CH2\u2013CH2\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)NH. I counted three CH2 groups between the alkyne and the carbonyl.\n- **Right end:** a tert-leucine linked to a 4-hydroxyproline, which is amidated by a 4-(4-methylthiazol-5-yl)benzylamine. This is the standard VHL ligand.\n\nStereochemistry is taken only from the three drawn wedge/hash centres: the tert-leucine \u03b1-carbon and the two hydroxyproline carbons. I set the SMILES chirality tags by comparing the neighbour order against the known VHL-ligand SMILES and permuting.\n\nSMILES: Oc1ccccc1-c1cc(N2CC3CCC(C2)N3c2ncc(C#CCCCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N3C[C@H](O)C[C@H]3C(=O)NCc3ccc(cc3)-c3scnc3C)cn2)c(N)nn1"
